{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","title":"Ray diagram for a converging lens"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A converging lens brings parallel light toward its far focus. Place an upright object six centimeters away; the focal length is two centimeters.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Converging lens"},{"op":"figure","id":"lens_diagram","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-7,5],"y":[-2.7,3.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"axis","from":[-6.7,0],"to":[4.7,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"param","id":"lens","x":"0.18*cos(t)","y":"2.7*sin(t)","t":[0,6.283185307179586]},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"point","id":"near_focus","at":[-2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"far_focus","at":[2,0],"label":"F′"},{"kind":"point","id":"object_base","at":[-6,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"object_tip","at":[-6,2]},{"kind":"segment","id":"object_arrow","from":{"at":"object_base"},"to":{"at":"object_tip"},"arrow":true,"label":"object"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"focal_value","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"f=2\\,\\text{cm},\\qquad u=6\\,\\text{cm}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From the object's tip, draw a ray parallel to the axis. After the lens, it travels through the far focus.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel_ray","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"lens_hit","at":[0,2]},{"kind":"segment","id":"incoming","from":{"at":"object_tip"},"to":{"at":"lens_hit"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"lens_hit"},"to":[4,-2],"arrow":true}]},{"op":"text","id":"ray_rule","anchor":{"el":"focal_value","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Parallel ray → far focus"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A second ray passes straight through the lens center. Where the rays meet, draw the image: real, inverted, and smaller.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"image_build","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"central_ray","from":{"at":"object_tip"},"to":[4,-1.3333333333333333],"arrow":true},{"kind":"point","id":"image_tip","at":{"hit":["refracted","central_ray"]}},{"kind":"point","id":"image_base","at":[3,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"image_arrow","from":{"at":"image_base"},"to":{"at":"image_tip"},"arrow":true,"label":"image"}]},{"op":"text","id":"image_type","anchor":{"el":"ray_rule","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Real, inverted, smaller"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why is this image real rather than virtual?","expected_gist":"The outgoing rays actually meet."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The lens equation confirms an image three centimeters away. Its magnification is negative one-half: inverted, and half the object's height.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"distance_marks","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[-6,-2.3],"to":[0,-2.3],"label":"6 cm"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-2.3],"to":[3,-2.3],"label":"3 cm"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"lens_equation","anchor":{"el":"image_type","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{f}-\\frac{1}{u}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad v=3\\,\\text{cm}"},{"op":"equation","id":"magnification","anchor":{"el":"lens_equation","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"m=-\\frac{v}{u}=-\\frac{3}{6}=-\\frac{1}{2}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.done","request_id":"ce5197dd-1366-49ba-8c1b-411c4cba2e60","accepted_steps":4,"repairs":0,"dropped_steps":0,"sanitized_steps":0,"sanitized_fields":0}
